			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Correct ViewContainersRegistry registry ID in ViewRegistrySnapshot\n\nThe ViewRegistrySnapshot diagnostic function was reporting containers=0\nbecause it used a guessed registry ID 'workbench.view.containersRegistry'\nwhich returned null from Registry.as(). The correct stock VS Code registry\nID (documented in vs/workbench/common/views.ts:35) is\n'workbench.registry.view.containers'. This fixes SkyBridge's diagnostic\nprobe so it now correctly reports the actual container and view counts\nfor extension manifests (Roo, Claude, gitlens, ...) reaching the workbench.",
			"SHA": "1f47ba960742d3e508694b6d695fb5174466af89"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T18:37:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				270,
				1
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "8990969b75a5f51a932dca0721304cf14a075ac9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T18:37:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				270,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Disable PatchTerminalGpuAcceleration, add ViewRegistrySnapshot\n\nTwo changes to the Output build pipeline:\n\n1. Remove PatchTerminalGpuAcceleration from BuildPipeline default order.\n   The transform fixed WebGL atlas font glitches (Menlo loading race) but\n   introduced a \"black shadow over text\" artifact from xterm's DOM-renderer\n   cursor/accessibility layer in WKWebView. Keeping the transform file on\n   disk for potential re-enablement after the input race fix lands.\n\n2. Add ViewRegistrySnapshot() to __CEL_SERVICES__ facade. This diagnostic\n   function queries the workbench's ViewContainersRegistry and ViewsRegistry\n   to return container/view counts + sample IDs. SkyBridge uses this to\n   verify extension manifests (Roo, Claude, gitlens) reached\n   viewsExtensionPoint's setHandler - the most common cause of silent\n   extension panel failures is contributions never flowing through\n   IExtensionService to the registry.",
			"SHA": "325a4de7ad74ebc36c42725572c9f36d4d7b8c3f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T17:42:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				270,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add PatchTerminalGpuAcceleration transform for WKWebView terminal\n\nAdd a new transform plugin that patches the terminal configuration schema to default `terminal.integrated.gpuAcceleration` to `'off'` instead of stock VS Code's `'auto'`. Under WKWebView, xterm.js's WebGL renderer builds its texture atlas before the Menlo font resolves, causing wrong cell widths and rendering glitches (overlapping characters, double-width glyph gaps, halos around anti-aliased edges due to texImage2D premultiplication differences).\n\nThe transform is currently NOT wired into the BuildPipeline by default. It was disabled after enabling revealed a \"black shadow over text\" artifact from xterm's DOM-renderer cursor/accessibility layer in WKWebView. The transform exists on disk so it can be re-enabled if the original WebGL atlas font drift issue resurfaces after the deferred-create race fix lands.\n\nUsers can still opt into WebGL by setting `terminal.integrated.gpuAcceleration: \"on\"` in settings.json — the schema enum is unchanged.",
			"SHA": "8d7a19d0e4241a66065c7e53257283843fae4c27"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T05:25:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				267,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Output): Rewrite CHANGELOG to document v2.x release chain\n\nComprehensive CHANGELOG rewrite documenting Output's evolution from v0.0 through v2.2. Adds new sections for the three v2.x releases:\n\n- v2.2: ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform, service-IIFE wrapping for bundled profile, Mountain→Cocoon buffer decoding, JSDoc nested comment fixes\n- v2.1: Polyfill hardening (6 Electron-to-Tauri shims, TauriMainProcessService IPC adapter, DevLog/Trace/telemetry)\n- v2.0: Source compilation migration from prebuilt artifacts to compiling from Dependency/Microsoft/Dependency/Editor/src\n\nRestructures older v1.x entries and adds inception details for v0.0-v0.2. Previously the changelog only documented up to v2.0 with minimal detail.",
			"SHA": "214a9ffb6fc64120ec88a3635c37af8be60d74db"
		}
	],
